        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Temperature / fever"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Afebrile."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pain for approximately 5–6 days, starting as a mild ache on waking and worsening, with a marked flare over the last 24–48 hours. Sharp and grabbing with movement. Anterolateral right shoulder pain radiating to the mid-humerus, not past the elbow. Severity 7–8/10 with movement and 3/10 at rest. Worse at night; unable to lie on the right side and struggling to sleep. Worse with overhead reach, putting on a jumper, reaching behind the back, reaching across the body, and hanging washing. Improved by keeping the arm by the side; heat pack helps a bit."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated symptoms and relevant negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No trauma, fall, or heavy lifting. No neck pain, paraesthesiae, chest pain, shortness of breath, fevers, sweats, weight loss, redness, or swelling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder inspection and palpation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No deformity, swelling, or erythema. Mild tenderness at the anterolateral acromion / greater tuberosity."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder range of motion"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Active flexion approximately 120 degrees, limited by pain. Abduction approximately 90–100 degrees, with painful arc approximately 60–120 degrees. Internal rotation limited behind the back; unable to reach bra strap. Passive range of motion near full with pain but no hard stop."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder strength and provocative tests"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Supraspinatus testing reproduces pain, with possible slight weakness versus pain inhibition. Infraspinatus and subscapularis strength grossly okay. Hawkins positive, Neer positive, painful arc positive."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Cervical spine and upper limb neurovascular examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Cervical spine full range of motion with no reproduction of pain. Upper limb neurovascular examination intact."
      }
    },
    {
